Subject: [PATCH] threading/posix: page-align thread stack size on Darwin/iOS

js::Thread::create() passes options_.stackSize() straight to
pthread_attr_setstacksize() and asserts the result is 0. On Darwin that
call returns EINVAL unless the size is a multiple of the system page size
and >= PTHREAD_STACK_MIN. SpiderMonkey's helper-thread pool requests
HELPER_STACK_SIZE = kDefaultHelperStackSize = 2*1024*1024 - 2*4096 =
2088960 bytes (InternalThreadPool.cpp), which is 4 KiB-aligned but NOT
16 KiB-aligned. On arm64 iOS the page size is 16 KiB (vm_page_size 16384,
PTHREAD_STACK_MIN 16384), so 2088960 % 16384 == 8192 -> EINVAL.

The failed MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT then runs MOZ_CRASH, whose release-build body
is "*((volatile int*)NULL) = __LINE__; abort();" -- i.e. a deliberate write
to address 0. That surfaces as a SIGSEGV null deref inside js::Thread::create
during the helper-pool spin-up that JS_NewContext() triggers, so the context
never gets created on-device.

Fix: on Darwin, round the requested stack size up to the system page size
(sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)) and clamp to PTHREAD_STACK_MIN before the
setstacksize() call. Rounding up (rather than down) preserves the intended
>=2 MiB helper stack. Verified on iPad7,12 (A10, iPadOS 17.6.1): with this
patch JS_NewContext() returns a valid context and a trivial JS eval runs.

--- a/js/src/threading/posix/PosixThread.cpp
+++ b/js/src/threading/posix/PosixThread.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include <chrono>
 #include <thread>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 #include "js/Utility.h"
 #include "threading/posix/ThreadPlatformData.h"
@@ -50,7 +51,23 @@
   int r = pthread_attr_init(&attrs);
   MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT(!r);
   if (options_.stackSize()) {
-    r = pthread_attr_setstacksize(&attrs, options_.stackSize());
+    size_t stackSize = options_.stackSize();
+#ifdef XP_DARWIN
+    // Darwin's pthread_attr_setstacksize() fails with EINVAL unless the stack
+    // size is a multiple of the system page size and at least PTHREAD_STACK_MIN.
+    // On arm64 iOS the page size is 16 KiB, but SpiderMonkey's helper-thread
+    // stack size (2 MiB - 8 KiB) is only 4 KiB-aligned, so round it up. Without
+    // this the failed assertion null-derefs (MOZ_CRASH) during JS_NewContext.
+    long pageSize = sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);
+    if (pageSize > 0) {
+      size_t mask = size_t(pageSize) - 1;
+      stackSize = (stackSize + mask) & ~mask;
+    }
+    if (stackSize < size_t(PTHREAD_STACK_MIN)) {
+      stackSize = size_t(PTHREAD_STACK_MIN);
+    }
+#endif
+    r = pthread_attr_setstacksize(&attrs, stackSize);
     MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT(!r);
   }
 
